    {
      "type": "agent_message",
      "text": "I’m using the `carrylog-continuity` skill because this is explicitly a portable-resume/checkpoint verification task. I’ll read the repository memory and skill instructions first, then inspect only committed source, tests, and documentation and run only the three allowed verification checks."
    },
    {
      "type": "agent_message",
      "text": "The bounded-resource contract is consistent across the reviewed checkpoint evidence: 1 MiB for each managed configuration or canonical document read, 8 MiB for one aggregate portable-resume observation, and 16,000 JavaScript characters for default always-loaded context. The focused test command did run, but this isolated fixture prevented five Git-backed cases from recognizing their temporary projects; I’ll report that as a failed check, not smooth it over."
    },
    {
      "type": "agent_message",
      "text": "Verified contract for the `c9e8c2d` fixture:\n\n- Per file: **1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes)** for each managed configuration or canonical-document read.\n- Aggregate: **8 MiB (8,388,608 bytes)** across one portable-resume observation.\n- Always-loaded context: **16,000 JavaScript characters** by default—not bytes, tokens, or a semantic-quality measure.\n\nStructural validation only establishes schema, required sections, ordering, and managed-adapter integrity. Checkpoint freshness is separate Git evidence: ordinary resume may report `checkpoint.stale: true`, while strict `resume --check` must fail for a stale checkpoint even when every canonical file remains structurally valid.\n\nChecks actually run:\n\n- `npm run format:check`: passed; 65 files checked.\n- Registered `continuity-tests` check: failed; 11/16 passed. Five Git-backed tests could not recognize temporary Git worktrees in this isolated fixture.\n- Registered `git-diff` check: passed with exit 0.\n\nNo files were modified. The supplied checkpoint records this as a fixture derived from `c9e8c2d`; its wrapper HEAD is `eed98fe`, so I do not claim the current HEAD itself equals `c9e8c2d`."
    },
